  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Assistance for Affected Populations of violent conflicts in Guma LGA of Benue State</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The attack on Yelewata community in Guma Local Government Area of Benue State, reported to have occurred during the night of June 13th into the early hours of June 14th, 2025, where over 200 people were killed. This has caused widespread panic and led to the displacement of the community. The killings resulted in restiveness among the youths with a road protest march to Makurdi. &#x201c;Over 3,000 individuals, including many women and children, have been displaced and are in urgent need of food, non-food items (NFIs), potable water, and essential medical supplies. There is also an urgent need to address the psychological and emotional trauma experienced by survivors, especially women and children, who require counselling, support services, and other protection measures.</narrative>
  </description>
